# Six on PC

Does GTA VI run on PC yet? Six on PC tracks every community effort to get the game running on PC, documents how far
the reverse engineering of its engine has got, and gives modders a reference to work from while they wait.

**Website:** [sixonpc.com](https://sixonpc.com) · **Forum:** [Discussions](https://github.com/Github-Samuel/sixonpc/discussions) · **Feed:** [RSS](https://sixonpc.com/feed.xml)

No game files, keys or executables are hosted or linked here. Links go to source code, documentation and news
reporting only.

## What it gives you

| If you want to | Go to |
| --- | --- |
| See how far GTA VI on PC has come, as one number | [The front page](https://sixonpc.com/) |
| Know which builds are playable, and who is closest | [The board](https://sixonpc.com/board) |
| Watch the builds running | [Footage](https://sixonpc.com/footage) |
| Look up a script native, its hash, parameters and an example | [Natives reference](https://sixonpc.com/natives) |
| See how much of your FiveM script depends on FiveM | [Port checker](https://sixonpc.com/natives/port?sample) |
| Turn a hash from a dump back into a name | [Hash lab](https://sixonpc.com/natives/lab) |
| Find out which file formats are cracked and what is still open | [RE status](https://sixonpc.com/status) |
| Check whether a "GTA VI for PC" repo is a fake | [Fake check](https://sixonpc.com/check) |
| Follow milestones and takedowns without checking back | [What changed](https://sixonpc.com/changes) and the [RSS feed](https://sixonpc.com/feed.xml) |
| Find a tool that opens an archive, texture, audio bank or video | [Tools](https://sixonpc.com/tools) |

Press <kbd>Ctrl</kbd> <kbd>K</kbd> anywhere on the site to search pages, port projects, tools, glossary terms and
all 14,776 natives at once.

## Overall progress

The top of the front page is one percentage for the whole field: the best any build has shown on each block of
the ladder (see Scoring), added up. Next to it: what the leading build does right now, the four numbers that
matter (best fps, builds you can walk around in, builds in the world, repos taken down), the curve since the
leak, the ladder as a coloured bar, and the milestones in the order they fell (first menus, first player moving,
prologue cleared, first kill, near-retail picture, 10 fps, 30 fps, story finished).

## Footage

Clips, streams and screenshots of each build, embedded or linked from where their creators posted them. Nothing
is copied to this site. The scout checks every YouTube, Rumble and GitHub item each hour; a clip taken down by a
DMCA claim stays listed as taken down. Filter by build, or open a board row to see that build's footage.

## The board

<a href="https://sixonpc.com/board"><img src="docs/screens/board.png" alt="The board: every GTA VI PC port effort ranked by progress"></a>

- Every port effort ranked by how far it gets with the game itself: boots, in the world, player moves, picture,
  story, speed and stability
- Private builds shown only on streams are listed too, marked as having no public code
- A "Spotted, not reviewed yet" list of new repos the scout finds each hour
- All projects plotted on one track, coloured by approach
- Stars, forks, commits, contributors and the latest commit from the GitHub API, refreshed every hour
- The top projects refresh live in the visitor's browser
- Search, filters and five sort orders
- Side-by-side comparison of two or three projects
- Starred projects and a "since you last looked" summary, stored in the browser

## Natives reference

<a href="https://sixonpc.com/natives/gta5/ENTITY/SET_ENTITY_COORDS"><img src="docs/screens/natives.png" alt="The natives browser showing SET_ENTITY_COORDS with its signature, hashes, parameters and example"></a>

Natives are the functions Rockstar's engine hands to scripts. No GTA VI native has been published yet, so this
starts from what the engine has always done.

- 6,701 GTA V natives, 7,132 Red Dead Redemption 2 natives and 943 Cfx natives
- Each native has its signature, hashes, parameter notes, written examples where they exist, and a generated call
  shape in Lua, JavaScript, C# and C++
- 2,074 natives appear in both GTA V and Red Dead Redemption 2. Rockstar kept those across two games, which marks
  them as engine and not game content, and makes them the first place to look in a third
- A three-pane browser with search by name or hash, filters, starred natives, keyboard navigation and a link per native
- Notes on what each of the 93 namespaces controls and what you see it do in game
- [GTA VI status](https://sixonpc.com/natives/vi): what is known about GTA VI natives, each finding marked as read at
  the source, reported or unverified. It shows zero mapped natives until someone publishes one with a method

### ROME blueprint

<a href="https://sixonpc.com/natives/rome"><img src="docs/screens/rome.png" alt="The ROME blueprint: Cfx natives grouped by the gap each fills"></a>

Rockstar has said nothing about how GTA VI will be scripted. What is on record is that its official Creator Platform
is FiveM and RedM. So the Cfx natives are sorted here by the gap each one fills in the base game: events, state bags,
resources, identity, routing, storage, UI, voice. It is a checklist of what any platform on this engine has to offer.

### Port checker

<a href="https://sixonpc.com/natives/port?sample"><img src="docs/screens/port.png" alt="The port checker sorting a sample script's natives into engine, GTA V only and FiveM only"></a>

Paste or drop a FiveM resource and every native it calls is sorted into five piles: engine natives, GTA V only,
platform layer, Cfx game extras and script runtime. It shows which calls lean on things known to move between games,
by line, and copies the result as Markdown. The script is read in the browser and never uploaded.

### Hash lab

<a href="https://sixonpc.com/natives/lab"><img src="docs/screens/lab.png" alt="The hash lab: joaat hasher, hash identification and table resolver"></a>

- Hash any name with joaat, lowercased or as written
- Identify a hash: a 64-bit native hash, a 32-bit hash in hex or decimal, or any spelling of a native name
- A dictionary of 497,914 names, 347 of them confirmed against real GTA VI data
- Paste up to 5,000 hashes from a native table, struct dump or archive listing and get names back for every known one

## Reverse-engineering status

<a href="https://sixonpc.com/status"><img src="docs/screens/status.png" alt="RE status: the unsolved problems, most blocking first"></a>

Running the game is one race. Understanding what is inside it is another, and mods depend on the second.

- 20 file formats and subsystems, each marked for whether the layout is documented, whether an open tool reads it,
  and whether two independent projects agree
- The unsolved problems, most blocking first, each with the best public lead. The first is locating the script bytecode
- Engine type names confirmed in the game's data, with their hashes
- Every row links to where the work is written up

### Names recovered here

The format notes quote hundreds of struct and field hashes with no name. We hashed 2.3 million identifiers from
public RAGE name lists, generated variants from the ones that matched, and put names on 78 of them, among them the
road graph structs (`CCoarsePathNode`, `CCoarsePathLink`) and the vehicle handling family (`ChassisHandlingData`,
`EngineHandlingData`, `DrivetrainHandlingData`). No game files were used. The list is on the
[status page](https://sixonpc.com/status#recovered), and the scripts and method are in
[`research/names`](research/names).

