## Stack

React 19, TypeScript and Vite, deployed as a static site on Vercel. No backend: `scout.mjs` builds one JSON file
from the GitHub API and the site reads it.

```
src/
  main.tsx          routes and app shell
  data.ts           types, constants, data loading
  components.tsx    track, podium, project row, compare, tool card, thread list
  pages/            Home, Board, Tools, Forum, Status, Changes (and reports), RepoCheck, More (estimate, fake check, story)
  re/formats.ts     the format status data, every row sourced
  styles.css        the original layout rules
  theme.css         the current look, loaded on top
  Palette.tsx       site-wide search on Ctrl K
  natives/          the natives reference: data loader, browser, pages, namespace notes
public/natives/     the native index and one detail file per namespace, built by natives.mjs
public/hashes/      the name dictionary in 256 shards, built by hashes.mjs
docs/screens/       the screenshots in this README
research/names/     scripts and results for recovering names from published hashes
public/data.json    the snapshot the site ships with
scout.mjs           builds data.json from the GitHub API
natives.mjs         builds public/natives from the public native databases
hashes.mjs          builds public/hashes from the gta6-namehash dictionary
```

## Run it locally

Needs Node 20 or newer.

```
git clone https://github.com/Github-Samuel/sixonpc
cd sixonpc
npm install
npm run dev
```

## Refresh the data

```
npm run scout
```

`scout.mjs` uses `GITHUB_TOKEN` if set, or the GitHub CLI login if `gh` is installed. Everything kept by hand is
in `board.mjs`: the project list with each build's milestone assessment, the tools list, footage, the milestone
dates, the lookalike and discovery search terms. Edit it there when a build moves, a clip appears or a tool is
missing.

Besides the GitHub numbers, each run also reads Take-Two's notices from GitHub's public DMCA repository, headlines
from Google News, checks that every piece of footage is still up, and searches for new repos that look like port
work.

The `Refresh data` workflow runs the scout every hour and pushes the result to the `data` branch. The site
loads that file at runtime and uses it when it is newer than the bundled snapshot, so the board stays current
without a redeploy.

## Rebuild the natives

```
npm run natives
```

`natives.mjs` downloads the public native databases, merges them and writes `public/natives`. Downloads are cached in
`.cache/natives`; pass `--fresh` to fetch them again. What is known about GTA VI is kept by hand in
`src/natives/vi.ts`, and every entry there needs a source.

## Rebuild the hash dictionary

```
npm run hashes
```

`hashes.mjs` downloads [gta6-namehash](https://github.com/tarekmania/gta6-namehash) (MIT) and splits it into 256 shards
by the first byte of the hash, so a lookup downloads about 50 KB and not 16 MB.

## Alerts

The scout writes `feed.xml` next to `data.json` on the `data` branch. To also post changes to Discord, add a
repository secret called `DISCORD_WEBHOOK` holding a channel webhook URL. Without it the step does nothing.

## Deploy

```
npm run build
vercel deploy --prod
```

## Scoring

| Points | Block |
| --- | --- |
| 20 | Boots: groundwork, the executable runs, first frames, menus |
| 10 | In the open world |
| 10 | A player you can move |
| 12 | Picture: from black to retail |
| 8 | Story: from the prologue to the credits |
| 30 | Speed: frames per second in the world, out of 30 |
| 10 | Stability: from crashing in minutes to never |

Half-working steps count for half. A build's score is its own; the overall figure takes the best any build has
shown on each block. Most results are reported by the projects themselves, and rows backed by a capture or a
stream are marked "shown on video". If a score is wrong, post in the forum with a link to the evidence.

## Credits

A good share of the tools list was first collected in
[awesome-gta6-reverse-engineering](https://github.com/Ahmet-Dedeler/awesome-gta6-reverse-engineering).

The GTA V and Red Dead Redemption 2 native data comes from alloc8or's NativeDB
([gta5-nativedb-data](https://github.com/alloc8or/gta5-nativedb-data),
[rdr3-nativedb-data](https://github.com/alloc8or/rdr3-nativedb-data)). Descriptions and examples for GTA V and all Cfx
natives come from the [Cfx.re native reference](https://github.com/citizenfx/natives).

The hash dictionary is [gta6-namehash](https://github.com/tarekmania/gta6-namehash) by tarekmania. The format status
page summarises the work of the projects it links to, chiefly
[GTA6-Asset-Info](https://github.com/TrinitronClient/GTA6-Asset-Info), [rage9-re](https://github.com/Ahmet-Dedeler/rage9-re)
and [leonidaforge/research](https://github.com/leonidaforge/research).

